WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.260
Hey, welcome to Platonet Terrianne Daily, episode 59, coming to you on May 10, 2026.

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:11.480
Here's what's new in science, health, and longevity research.

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:18.360
A neural break on scratching has been found that prevents over scratching once its relief begins.

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:24.840
Researchers trace the break to the ion channel TRPV4 in sensory neurons.

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:29.040
In mice lacking this channel, overall scratching dropped.

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:35.320
Yet the animals kept going longer once they started, which shows the molecule normally limits

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:41.740
itch-driven behavior. The finding comes from chronic itch models and points to a targeted

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:47.760
mechanism for conditions like eczema. Instead of suppressing the immune system broadly,

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:52.840
therapies could focus on restoring or mimicking this internal off switch.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:01:00.620
The TRPV4 channel functions as a molecular timer that tells sensory neurons when scratching

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:07.960
has gone far enough. In chronic itch-states, loss of this signal leaves the system unable to stop

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:13.660
even after relief arrives, which explains why some patients scratch until skin is damaged.

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:20.040
What other common sensations might be kept in check by similar timers that remain unmapped?

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:27.580
Now shifting to atmosphere chemistry, the 2022 hunger-tongue eruption destroyed large amounts

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:34.540
of atmospheric methane. Volcanic ash, seawater salts, and sunlight generated from maldehyde

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:40.120
and reactive chlorine that rapidly broke down methane released during the event itself.

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:46.780
The process shows how a single underwater eruption can alter global atmosphere composition

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:52.660
on a short time scale. Current climate models do not yet include this kind of sudden chemical

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:59.040
sink, which leaves open questions about how future volcanic activity might offset or interact with

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:05.580
human emissions. The result adds a new variable to methane budgets that scientists will need to track

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:12.740
more closely. On a different note, hidden channels beneath our Antarctic ice shelves are accelerating

00:02:12.740 --> 00:02:18.840
melting in ways current models miss. Warm ocean water becomes trapped in long cavities,

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:26.020
carved under floating ice, which intensifies basal melt from below. Because this process is

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:32.360
not represented in most projections, estimates of future sea level rise are likely too low.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:39.220
The finding comes from direct observations of ice shelf hydrology and highlights how small scale

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:46.120
fluid dynamics can scale up to affect coastlines worldwide. Researchers are now working to

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:53.020
incorporate these channels into larger ice sheet simulations. Next up, time delivery of two

00:02:53.020 --> 00:03:00.840
growth factors restored digit regrowth in adult mice after amputation. Sequential application of FGF

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:08.360
two followed by BMP2 allowed bone and soft teaching to reform in ways that do not normally occur

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:16.360
in mammals. The Nature Communications Study demonstrates that adult mammalian tissue retains latent

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:23.700
regenerative capacity when given the right molecular cues at the right times. This is not yet a

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:29.620
therapy for humans, but it opens a route for stimulating limited repair after injury or surgery.

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:37.140
The work sits in regenerative biology rather than drug development and focuses on the sequence of

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:44.100
signals rather than a single compound. Moving to diagnostics, retinal imaging can detect multiple

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:51.320
systemic diseases beyond the eye itself. Patterns in the retina were linked to several non-ocular

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:58.540
conditions in a new analysis, offering a non-invasive screening route. Most people assume an eye exam

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:07.200
only checks how well you see or whether you need new glasses. In reality, the retina is an extension

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:12.700
of the central nervous system that shares blood supply and cellular features with the brain and

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:19.560
other organs. Right now, as you listen, light sensitive cells in your retina are already exposing

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:25.800
subtle changes in blood vessel structure and nerve layer thickness that can signal diabetes,

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:35.640
hypertension or early neurododideration. A single high-resolution scan captures roughly 100,000

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:42.380
individual data points across multiple layers, far more information than a standard blood pressure

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:48.620
reading. Because the retina sits behind a clear optical window, these measurements require

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:54.680
no needles or radiation. Clinicians are beginning to use the same images to track treatment

00:04:54.680 --> 00:05:00.940
or response in conditions far from the eye. And upcoming studies will combine retinal imaging

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:08.260
with AI to flag cardiovascular risk years before symptoms appear. The approach could eventually

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:14.160
replace some blood test or distant imaging for routine screening. Turning to genetics,

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:20.920
intrinsic human lifespan heritability reaches roughly 50 percent once shared environment and

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:26.760
lifestyle are properly controlled for. A science study refined earlier estimates that had been

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:33.180
inflated by unaccounted confounders. The result clarifies that genetics explain about half the

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:39.600
variation in how long people live, while the rest remains open to behavioral and environmental

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:46.460
influence. This adjusted figure gives researchers a clearer target when studying the biological

00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:52.260
limits of health span. It also underscores that longevity is not purely inherited,

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:59.040
and that interventions can still move the needle for most individuals. In gut health research,

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:06.240
a black licorice compound reduced intestinal damage in inflammatory bowel disease models, fast.

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:14.560
Using stem cell derived human intestinal tissue, researchers screen thousands of compounds and

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:21.780
identify glyceryzen as an anti-inflammatory candidate. The molecule lowered cell death and tissue

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:28.640
injury in both the lab model and in mice. The work shows how organoid platforms can accelerate

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:35.160
discovery of compounds already present in the food supply. It remains early stage, yet it points

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:42.400
toward new ways to protect mecosyl tissue without broad immunosuppression. Finally, psychedelic

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:49.140
assisted therapy was linked to reduce severe depression in real world data. Patients receiving

00:06:49.140 --> 00:06:56.780
structured psychotherapy plus LSD or psilocybin showed substantial and lasting drops in depression

00:06:56.780 --> 00:07:04.280
and anxiety scores. The observational findings add support for lasting clinical benefit when these

00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:10.820
compounds are paired with therapy rather than used in isolation. The data come from clinical

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:16.860
settings where dosing and psychological support were carefully managed. While not a randomized

00:07:16.860 --> 00:07:22.180
trial, the results strengthen the case for continued controlled investigation of these approaches.

